# Who builds the backdrop? Right after the level is unpacked ($9130, before
# the loader calls $8C94, $77E2, $1DA2), arm one-shot watches on a long past the
# stored backdrop ($6D500) and one inside it ($69A00). --trace fdc.
expect prompt read sector sector=0x1 .*tr=0x0 .*addr=0x6760e
stage backdrop-arm.ini
stage backdrop-hit.ini
debug b pc = $9130 :once :trace :file {run}/backdrop-arm.ini
disk-a {disk2}
sleep 8
fire
sleep 4
fire
expect level1-read read sector sector=0x3 .*tr=0xc .*addr=0x3e
quiet level1-loaded 3
fire
sleep 2
fire
sleep 4
